course: dictionary
lesson: 7189
title: Persuasive writing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Persuasive means good at making people agree with you or do what you want. A persuasive speaker can change the minds of the people listening.
explain: Persuasive writing is writing that tries to make the reader believe something or take an action. Adverts, letters of complaint and speeches all try to persuade you. «A persuasive text tries to change your mind.»
explain: Writers use clues to persuade you. They give a clear opinion, reasons, facts and numbers, and a strong ending. When you read an advert, ask yourself: is it giving reasons, or only trying to make me feel excited?
fact: Persuasive means good at making people agree with you or do what you want.
fact: «A persuasive letter states what the writer wants, gives reasons and evidence, and stays polite.»
fact: Persuasive writing tries to make the reader agree or do something.
fact: Every piece of writing has a job, and persuasive writing tries to change your mind.
fact: Adverts use persuasive language and slogans; «bussin'» is Gen Z slang meaning really good.
exercise: «A persuasive text tries to change your mind.» What is the job of a persuasive text? | To tell you how to build a shed | *To make the reader agree or do something | To explain what a volcano is | To list the weather for the week
exercise: Which of these is persuasive writing? | A list of bus times | *A speech asking everyone to recycle, with reasons | A weather report for Monday | A recipe for pancakes
exercise: Which word means good at making people agree with you? | Careful | *Persuasive | Ancient | Curious
test: Maya wants a puppy, so she writes a list of reasons and asks her mum politely. What kind of writing is this? | Instructions | *Persuasive writing | An explanation | A report
test: Which thing does a persuasive letter always do? | Draw pictures | Use rhyming lines | *State clearly what the writer wants | Tell a made-up story
exam: Which sentence is persuasive? | The bus leaves at nine | The river is 40 km long | *You should join our club, because it is fun and free | Water boils at 100 degrees
